{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415921-v5-fixing-frenzy","id":1415921,"title":"[V5] Fixing Frenzy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-28T19:04:56-07:00","id":1415921,"title":"[V5] Fixing Frenzy","content":"<br /> In my chronicle, bestial crits seem to happen in combat quite often. In such situations, it feels natural for them to mean that the player character goes into frenzy - but then the player lose control over their character, and don't get to play them. I think that's boring. I wanna come up with something better.<br /> <br /> How can I make frenzy a state that limits how you can play your character, or costs you something, rather than hands the character over to the gamemaster? I was gonna post this question on a Swedish discussion board first, because people there are so good with rules systems...but I then thought you guys might have interesting ideas, too, being Vampire experts after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Random ideas:<br /> <br /> what if you never suffer stains while frenzying? This would encourage players to really go all out. Maybe each stain you would suffer instead becomes willpower damage? But then there needs to be some other reward for doing bestial things when frenzying, the encouragement isn't great enough.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, perhaps the opposite - each stain you suffer while frenzying gives you back willpower? Still not compelling enough perhaps, because stains are such a dangerous currency that just taking one is quite a lot...<br /> <br /> Other variants would be more &quot;sophisticated&quot;, Kindred of the East-style frenzies, like your convictions being reversed, or having an extra set of convictions and desires for frenzy mode. Hmm...I like the latter idea there...it would mean you get away with more while frenzying, and you could regain more willpower by trying to fulfil your frenzy desire - which would of course be something dreadful.<br /> <br /> <br /> Please don't answer this thread if you have nothing to contribute except telling me how wrong I am trying to change the Frenzy concept. I'm interested in <i>how</i> to do it, not whether I <i>should</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","user":"Natsymir","date":". 09-28-2020, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T21:07:45-07:00","id":1415930,"title":"","content":"Two ways I do it.<br /> <br /> One, just let the player portray their character during the frenzy. Tell the player what the Beast makes their PC do (&quot;you pounce on your dear doting mother and attempt to suck her veins dry&quot;), but let them roll the dice and roleplay it out.<br /> <br /> Two, just fast forward to whenever the vampire snaps out of frenzy. Have the player roll whatever dice they need to roll, and describe their gore-streaked surroundings when they come to. The way I've always seen it, vampires don't remember what happens when the Beast takes over. They aren't in the driver's seat. All conscious thought recedes while the Beast is out playing. <br /> <br /> There's no way I'd run an extended scene where it's me playing the frenyzing PC and the player sitting on their hands. Complete waste of everyone's time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T21:13:59-07:00","id":1415931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415921-v5-fixing-frenzy?p=1415930#post1415930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two ways I do it.<br /> <br /> One, just let the player portray their character during the frenzy. Tell the player what the Beast makes their PC do (&quot;you pounce on your dear doting mother and attempt to suck her veins dry&quot;), but let them roll the dice and roleplay it out.<br /> <br /> Two, just fast forward to whenever the vampire snaps out of frenzy. Have the player roll whatever dice they need to roll, and describe their gore-streaked surroundings when they come to. The way I've always seen it, vampires don't remember what happens when the Beast takes over. They aren't in the driver's seat. All conscious thought recedes while the Beast is out playing.<br /> <br /> There's no way I'd run an extended scene where it's me playing the frenyzing PC and the player sitting on their hands. Complete waste of everyone's time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've also done both of those approaches, but the thing is, I'm not completely satisfied with them. I'd like something with more game mechanics tied into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T21:22:00-07:00","id":1415933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415921-v5-fixing-frenzy#post1415921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can I make frenzy a state that limits how you can play your character, or costs you something, rather than hands the character over to the gamemaster?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's your goal with frenzy mechanics then? Because the GM telling you how you can portray your character seems like it accomplishes all of those things already. <br /> <br /> One thing I will say so far as costs is that not all frenzies are created equal. Frenzying because a rival you already hate was taunting you is a completely different scenario from frenzying in front of the prince or your dear doti\u200bng mother. Most of the time in my experience, players would rather just not frenzy than get a Willpower or stain immunity in compensation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T00:34:25-07:00","id":1415948,"title":"","content":"This is not exactly about the frenzy rules, but may be could help you. You said you get a lot of bestial crits during combat, in that cases I prefer not to send the PC to frenzy, instead I look for a penalty in their success. An easy aproach I like to use force the attack into an All-Out attack (see page 298). Depenging on the situation you could also make them unarmed becouse they broke their weapon during the attack or get it stuck in the opponents body or simply give them some stains if appropiate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25915-nicolai","name":"nicolai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T08:36:06-07:00","id":1415983,"title":"","content":"Frenzies should proabably cause stains since Wassail is the FINAL Frenzy<br /> <br /> That being said I'd give the characters bonuses for being in frenzy Given them a bunch more dice on all actions. Let them play it out Hell make it super optimal to drop into Frenzy for combat. That those who don't generally don't do as well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T15:02:12-07:00","id":1416034,"title":"","content":"My main question would be, why are you making Messy Criticals worse than they are? A messy critical is not a Frenzy in function; it is a brief, seconds-lapse in control that generally results in something destructive happening because the Beast 'helps out', but you still get your goal. Making it into a full blown Frenzy ultimately removes your success angle. <br /> <br /> You could also go with some options that even the devs have said they'd do, such as push a Clan Compulsion as a Messy Critical outcome (since it's still the Beast/their vampiric nature winning out), or go with the obvious supernatural outcome (they tear apart a shelf of books, damaging them, but find the one they want; or they stealth like a goddamn hunting cat, moving inhumanly, those sorts of things).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T16:10:51-07:00","id":1416041,"title":"","content":"<b>Vampires must be functional</b><br /> If we want to play monsters that hide among their own prey they must be able to fake being human or otherwise there is no masquerade.<br /> <br /> Messy Crits mechanics means in world that V5 vampires are always acting like crazy mofos and catching attention becuase unless they are at hunger 0 with by game design they will almost never be.<br /> <br /> They also take control from the player all the time becuase as you said is rare for them not to happen so....here is a nuclear question is if a mechanic is plain bad why not ignore it?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T16:35:33-07:00","id":1416044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415921-v5-fixing-frenzy?p=1416041#post1416041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Vampires must be functional</b><br /> If we want to play monsters that hide among their own prey they must be able to fake being human or otherwise there is no masquerade.<br /> <br /> Messy Crits mechanics means in world that V5 vampires are always acting like crazy mofos and catching attention becuase unless they are at hunger 0 with by game design they will almost never be.<br /> <br /> They also take control from the player all the time becuase as you said is rare for them not to happen so....here is a nuclear question is if a mechanic is plain bad why not ignore it?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have a problem with this rule too. How am I going to find it good to lose background points or even worse fail the test instead of succeed just because of that damn hunger dice that I can't even get ride no matter how much blood I drink. Beast should be scary. If the Vampiric condition make you look like a clow follow Leandro advice and ignore it. If you are a player instead of st, bad luck to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T12:40:43-07:00","id":1416152,"title":"","content":"Good to know: before v5 The Beast was a simplistic creature who only cared for survival and, though it might overreact(murdering someone who insults you, running in fear from a cigarette lighter) wouldn't do anything uneccessary (killing efficiently, not making a mess for the sake of it)<br /> <br /> there were no messy crits, either you were in control or you'd failed and allowed It to usurp control. No grey area, it was black or white. The actions of the Beast were the actions of the Beast, yet it was your fault for allowing the situation to occur. If you had just managed things well it never would have had the chance to rear... unlike v5 where the beast is always active and screwing with you and you have virtually no agency concerning it. <br /> <br /> If you don't like the way V5 does the beast, consider going back in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T07:15:48-07:00","id":1416252,"title":"","content":"it's either a bestial failure or a messy crit, bestial crits aren't a thing. either way they don't inherently cause you to frenzy, so if you don't want them to frenzy then don't let them frenzy. simple as that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}